From: DroidDeck contributor
Subject: [PATCH] gamescope_<convar>=0 reads a bool convar as true

The environment override builds the Lua line `gamescope.convars.NAME.value = VALUE`. For a bool
convar, 0 and 1 are Lua numbers and every number is true, so `gamescope_composite_force=0` switched
the convar on; only `=false` switched it off. A number given to a bool convar now becomes `value ~= 0`.
Other convar types and `true`/`false` are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -924,7 +924,8 @@
 					std::string_view value( strtok( nullptr, "=" ) );
 					if ( script.Manager().Gamescope().Convars.Base[name].valid() )
 					{
-						auto override_script = std::format( "gamescope.convars.{}.value = {}", name, value );
+						auto override_script = std::format( "do local c = gamescope.convars.{0}; local v = {1}; "
+							"if type( c.value ) == 'boolean' and type( v ) == 'number' then v = ( v ~= 0 ) end; c.value = v end", name, value );
 						console_log.infof( "Overriding from environment variable: %s", override_script.c_str() );
 						script->script( override_script );
 					}
